// Mail bombing before a helpdesk call: the subject's inbound mail that Microsoft
// flagged, per hour, over the last 30 days. A bombing shows as one or two hours
// with 50-150 messages from as many different senders, mostly newsletter and
// mailing-list "confirm your subscription" mail in several languages, an hour or
// so before an outside Teams chat. Only messages with a threat verdict reach
// TIMailData, so this undercounts the flood; the shape still stands out against
// the subject's normal handful a day. Mail filtered by a gateway in front of
// Microsoft 365 (Proofpoint, Mimecast) never reaches it at all.
// Security-awareness simulations (KnowBe4 and similar) land here too: simSender
// counts them so they are not read as an attack.
// Placeholders: {UPN} = the subject's address, lower-cased.
Office365
| where timestamp > ago(30d)
| where Operation == "TIMailData" and tostring(Directionality) == "Inbound"
| where tolower(tostring(Recipients)) contains "{UPN}"
| extend p1 = tolower(tostring(P1Sender)), subj = tolower(tostring(Subject))
| summarize messages = dcount(tostring(NetworkMessageId)), senders = dcount(p1),
    subscriptionLike = dcountif(tostring(NetworkMessageId), subj contains "confirm" or subj contains "subscri"
        or subj contains "newsletter" or subj contains "registr" or subj contains "verif"),
    simSender = dcountif(tostring(NetworkMessageId), p1 contains "knowbe4" or p1 contains "phishsim"
        or p1 contains "phishme" or p1 contains "proofpointsecurityawareness"),
    sampleSubject = take_any(tostring(Subject))
    by hour = bin(timestamp, 1h)
| order by hour asc
| take 1000
